WEBVTT

00:01.790 --> 00:04.460
<i>We made it
to the Grand Finals on Oban,</i>

00:04.630 --> 00:07.340
<i>despite, well, everything.</i>

00:07.800 --> 00:10.050
<i>And Oban is a trip.</i>

00:10.260 --> 00:12.680
<i>Of course, we're not alone
in Wonderland.</i>

00:12.970 --> 00:14.720
<i>The eight other finalists
are here as well.</i>

00:15.060 --> 00:16.520
<i>A pretty scary bunch.</i>

00:16.810 --> 00:17.730
<i>Hey, whatever.</i>

00:18.060 --> 00:20.020
<i>We came for the Ultimate Prize.</i>

00:20.650 --> 00:23.820
<i>We're not going to roll over
and play dead for these aliens.</i>

00:24.900 --> 00:27.320
<i>That includes the good Prince Aikka.</i>

00:27.690 --> 00:30.450
<i>He's not the only one
who understands honor.</i>

01:55.910 --> 01:58.450
I can't believe this is
the same planet we landed on.

01:58.660 --> 02:00.830
It was just an endless desert.

02:01.500 --> 02:05.080
According to Koji, Oban is
much larger than our own sun.

02:05.250 --> 02:07.290
So we can expect some surprises.

02:07.670 --> 02:08.840
Let's check it out!

02:09.170 --> 02:11.300
Wait, shouldn't we tell Don Wei?

02:11.920 --> 02:13.590
Mr. Killjoy?

02:14.130 --> 02:15.050
<i>No.</i>

02:15.220 --> 02:17.220
We don't need a dad
to come along.

02:17.390 --> 02:18.180
Let's go.

02:27.270 --> 02:28.820
Run, humans.

02:28.980 --> 02:31.030
Run while you still can.

02:36.950 --> 02:39.280
Different region,
but just as many temples.

02:39.450 --> 02:41.370
Look, they're
everywhere around us.

02:41.540 --> 02:42.250
Yeah, I know.

02:42.910 --> 02:45.330
But whoever built them
is long gone.

02:51.170 --> 02:51.840
Molly!

02:52.590 --> 02:53.720
Wait!

03:06.310 --> 03:07.480
<i>Wow.</i>

03:13.490 --> 03:17.490
Like I said, these temples
have been abandoned for centuries.

03:17.660 --> 03:18.990
Pretty spooky, don't you think?

03:21.330 --> 03:22.120
Molly?

03:43.060 --> 03:44.930
Molly?
Are you up there?

04:18.430 --> 04:20.840
Jordan?
This isn't funny.

04:32.940 --> 04:34.780
I hope you're pleased
with yourself.

04:35.030 --> 04:36.530
I was scared, you know.

04:37.070 --> 04:38.030
What are you talking about?

04:38.200 --> 04:39.820
I've been looking
for you everywhere.

04:41.570 --> 04:43.280
I guess
that wasn't you after all.

04:44.280 --> 04:46.580
What do you say
we head back to the module.

04:47.040 --> 04:48.370
Like as fast as we can.

04:48.580 --> 04:50.290
Escape is pointless.

04:50.540 --> 04:52.250
You are at my mercy.

04:53.590 --> 04:55.380
Well that mystery is solved.

04:55.710 --> 04:58.050
You know, short stuff,
you almost scared us.

04:58.300 --> 05:00.340
I should have terrified you!

05:04.550 --> 05:06.720
For I am Lord Furter!

05:06.890 --> 05:10.310
Master Pirate
and King of the Seven Seas!

05:17.980 --> 05:20.360
Hey, what's the big idea,
little guys?

05:21.110 --> 05:24.490
Tie up these tourists and find
a deep hole to dump them in.

05:27.410 --> 05:30.370
You can't do that.
We're here to race like you.

05:30.620 --> 05:31.670
Exactly!

05:32.750 --> 05:35.340
How do you think we managed
to reach the Grand Finals?

05:36.750 --> 05:40.800
One less team means I'm one step
closer to my treasure.

05:41.090 --> 05:42.760
The Ultimate Prize!

05:46.390 --> 05:48.350
Come on, drop your weapons
and fight like men!

05:48.970 --> 05:50.560
I'll take you all on.

05:52.440 --> 05:53.100
Jordan!

05:53.270 --> 05:54.440
Ouch!

05:54.980 --> 05:56.060
That hurt.

06:02.110 --> 06:03.490
Leave me alone.

06:03.740 --> 06:04.740
Don't touch me!

06:04.910 --> 06:06.370
Let me go!

06:21.720 --> 06:24.840
Perfect. No one
will ever find them here.

06:25.340 --> 06:26.970
You wouldn't really
do that, would you?

06:27.140 --> 06:29.560
This is all a big joke, right?
You're playing with us.

06:31.220 --> 06:33.140
Farewell, my angel.

06:33.310 --> 06:36.650
I'll have a fond memory of you
when I win the Ultimate Prize.

06:37.480 --> 06:39.650
You're a monster!
A heartless monster!

06:42.190 --> 06:43.780
Thanks for the compliment.

06:47.910 --> 06:48.830
No!

06:49.120 --> 06:50.290
No, stop!

06:55.830 --> 06:57.540
Come on, men!
Do the deed.

07:11.640 --> 07:13.390
-Retreat!
-Back to the ship!

07:26.400 --> 07:27.240
Look out!

07:31.950 --> 07:33.410
Scrape the rope
against the rock.

07:33.580 --> 07:34.450
Quick!

07:36.210 --> 07:37.920
Come on! Faster! Come on!

08:34.010 --> 08:35.350
Come on.

08:35.970 --> 08:38.890
Let's split before our friends
heat up the cooking pot.

08:39.060 --> 08:40.560
I don't think
they'll harm us, Jordan.

08:48.610 --> 08:50.570
Well, I'm not sticking around
to find out.

08:58.710 --> 09:00.080
Listen. They've stopped.

09:00.670 --> 09:01.750
Huh? Run!

09:02.080 --> 09:03.500
They know we're gone.

09:03.670 --> 09:04.420
Hurry!

09:30.490 --> 09:33.280
Next time you're thinking
of going for a little stroll,

09:33.620 --> 09:34.740
you're on your own.

09:46.630 --> 09:49.460
I'm glad to see
you're both enjoying yourselves.

09:49.960 --> 09:52.680
Where on earth have you been?
We've been worried sick!

09:55.550 --> 09:58.930
Well, we've escaped an earthquake,
survived an alien ambush and...

09:59.350 --> 10:02.270
I'd advise you
not to take my authority lightly.

10:02.850 --> 10:05.610
Young lady, I am not here
for your childish stories.

10:05.770 --> 10:07.190
I'm here to win a race.

10:07.360 --> 10:10.030
The greatest race
of all, remember?

10:10.490 --> 10:12.780
-Yes sir. But we really did...
-Enough!

10:13.200 --> 10:15.410
Get to your positions
immediately.

10:15.570 --> 10:17.280
The second race
is about to begin.

10:17.990 --> 10:18.990
Yes, sir!

10:38.260 --> 10:39.600
We've increased
the thrust reactors,

10:39.810 --> 10:42.350
so you should have less
of a bumpy fall this time.

10:42.770 --> 10:44.810
And we've also fixed
the booster drives.

10:44.980 --> 10:46.440
But make sure
to use them sparingly

10:46.600 --> 10:49.360
or you'll be out of fuel in a snap.
The races are longer on Oban.

10:50.440 --> 10:51.280
Got it, Stan.

10:53.030 --> 10:54.950
Most of all, we need points.

10:55.110 --> 10:56.870
We must finish at least third.

10:57.030 --> 10:58.830
Do not come back without points!

11:02.700 --> 11:06.290
<i>The stakes
of this competition surpass us all.</i>

11:07.000 --> 11:08.670
Hey, don't mind Don Wei.

11:09.000 --> 11:10.880
He's worse
than Lord Furter sometimes.

11:11.340 --> 11:12.210
That's for sure.

11:12.380 --> 11:14.420
I'd rather be thrown
in a bottomless pit

11:14.590 --> 11:15.680
than listen to him.

11:16.430 --> 11:18.390
But he's right
about one thing, Jordan.

11:18.550 --> 11:20.260
We've got to start
scoring points.

11:20.430 --> 11:22.390
After all, these are
the Grand Finals.

11:23.390 --> 11:25.440
Buckle up and let's rock, partner.

11:26.980 --> 11:28.020
All right!

11:53.340 --> 11:54.880
First stone door located!

12:05.930 --> 12:07.980
You'll wish you'd never escaped!

12:12.900 --> 12:15.570
I've got a total
of five stone gates for today's race.

12:15.940 --> 12:16.900
Roger that.

12:19.860 --> 12:21.200
Go through this one first.

12:55.980 --> 12:58.150
Not today,
you won't, Prince Aikka.

13:13.880 --> 13:16.000
So long, pretty boy!
I'll send you a card.

13:25.350 --> 13:27.100
OK, you're in second place.

13:27.270 --> 13:29.850
But you still have
four more gates to go.

13:30.560 --> 13:32.690
Stan, Koji,
I think I saw something.

13:36.480 --> 13:37.860
What is that thing?

13:38.990 --> 13:40.700
Did you see anything
on your scanners?

13:41.200 --> 13:42.320
Nothing.
Whatever it was,

13:42.490 --> 13:44.740
it couldn't possibly keep up
with the Whizzing Arrow 3.

13:44.910 --> 13:45.910
Check again, Koji.

13:46.080 --> 13:47.740
Jordan, keep your eyes open

13:47.910 --> 13:50.160
and fire
at the first sign of hostility.

14:22.950 --> 14:25.280
Two more gates.
Here's our chance!

14:31.620 --> 14:35.540
<i>I can do it, Dad.
I know I can win this race.</i>

14:39.960 --> 14:43.590
<i>I'll get that Ultimate Prize
and I'll bring Maya back.</i>

14:59.190 --> 15:01.070
Where in the world
did that ship come from?

15:04.490 --> 15:06.570
It's not fast enough
to have gone through all the gates.

15:10.700 --> 15:11.580
Tell him that.

15:21.460 --> 15:23.260
They must have come
straight to this location.

15:24.760 --> 15:26.010
It's an ambush!

15:45.650 --> 15:47.660
Molly, get away from there.

16:04.960 --> 16:07.760
Hip hip hooray!
Long live Lord Furter!

16:10.600 --> 16:13.180
You'll make us both lose,
you fool! What are you doing?

16:13.430 --> 16:15.140
I'm boarding your ship.

16:15.640 --> 16:18.270
That's what pirates do.
They board ships.

16:23.520 --> 16:25.190
We were almost there.

16:27.950 --> 16:29.910
Today, the Earth team's ship.

16:30.070 --> 16:32.660
Tomorrow, the Ultimate Prize!

16:43.090 --> 16:44.500
Prepare to board!

16:44.670 --> 16:46.050
Attack!

17:08.070 --> 17:10.320
Jordan,
don't do anything stupid.

17:10.990 --> 17:12.110
Be careful.

17:14.950 --> 17:16.700
Any final words?

17:18.750 --> 17:21.870
You see, men?
His fear of us has turned him to stone.

17:24.250 --> 17:25.840
Molly, turn now!

18:11.010 --> 18:12.840
Ah! Oh my ship!

18:13.180 --> 18:15.300
My beautiful ship.

18:32.860 --> 18:34.660
No points once again.

18:35.320 --> 18:36.910
Missed our chance.

18:43.580 --> 18:45.210
What an amazing race.

18:45.370 --> 18:47.250
Never a dull moment around here.

18:50.760 --> 18:53.590
<i>Ning and Shun take
the high points from this race.</i>

18:53.760 --> 18:55.890
Just ahead of Ondai and Sul.

18:56.260 --> 19:00.140
After two races, Sul retains
the lead in the competition.

19:02.520 --> 19:04.520
All this excitement
has made me hungry.

19:05.440 --> 19:07.560
I think it's lunch time again!

19:25.330 --> 19:26.670
It was a bad day.

19:26.830 --> 19:28.670
Another bad day.

19:29.130 --> 19:31.170
Almost winning isn't enough.

19:31.340 --> 19:33.260
We came here to win.

19:33.630 --> 19:35.630
And we need to points to do so.

19:36.300 --> 19:39.140
At this rate, we'll never catch up
with the leaders.

19:43.390 --> 19:46.140
As long as we can fly,
we still have a chance.

19:50.150 --> 19:52.690
I refuse to believe
it's the end of the world.

20:01.410 --> 20:03.990
As long as we can fly,
we still have a chance.

20:04.370 --> 20:07.120
I refuse to believe
it's the end of the world.

20:27.140 --> 20:29.400
Molly, are you still up?

20:30.400 --> 20:32.150
No, I'm asleep.

20:32.770 --> 20:34.980
Are you still worried
about Don Wei?

20:35.570 --> 20:36.940
I'm just beginning
to understand

20:37.150 --> 20:39.740
Oban will be a lot
tougher than I thought.

20:40.780 --> 20:42.910
And that I...

20:43.580 --> 20:45.080
might never see my mom again.

20:47.660 --> 20:49.500
Hey Molly, relax.

20:49.670 --> 20:52.000
You said it yourself.
It was a bad day.

20:52.170 --> 20:53.380
I'm sure we'll be fine.

20:53.540 --> 20:55.170
You'll see your parents
soon enough.

20:55.340 --> 20:56.920
Probably too soon.

20:59.260 --> 21:02.930
Just imagine how they'll feel
when we return with the Ultimate Prize.

21:03.140 --> 21:05.010
All the big shots
will welcome us.

21:05.180 --> 21:07.390
Our parents won't
believe their eyes.

21:10.230 --> 21:11.560
Molly?
